 "intro": "Uxellodunum, a fortified town on cliffs above a river in south-western Gaul, 51 BC. The last Gallic rebels have taken refuge there with food for years. You are Julius Caesar.",
 "debrief": "In Hirtius’s account (the eighth book of Caesar’s Gallic War), Caesar posted archers and slingers to stop the defenders drawing water from the river, then built a terrace and a ten-storey tower to command the spring beneath the walls. The defenders rolled down burning barrels, but Caesar ordered attacks on every side to distract them. Finally his engineers tunnelled to the spring’s source and cut it, and the town surrendered. Caesar cut off the hands of all who had borne arms, as a warning to Gaul. The other choices are what-ifs.",
